From 0c9a1f072e07d33e2ec44b2d363f33e153f01972 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nick Kennedy <nick@nick-kennedy.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 00:22:06 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] kosmickrisp: add minimal VK_EXT_metal_objects

Advertise VK_EXT_metal_objects and implement the parts Monado's macOS
Vulkan client uses inside an app process:

- VkImportMetalTextureInfoEXT on vkCreateImage: adopt an existing
  MTLTexture (single plane, layout must match), add it to the device
  residency set, and treat vkBindImageMemory as a no-op for it.
- VkImportMetalIOSurfaceInfoEXT on vkCreateImage: create a 2D texture
  over a caller-supplied IOSurface (NULL IOSurface is not supported).
- VkImportMetalSharedEventInfoEXT on vkCreateSemaphore: back a timeline
  semaphore with the supplied MTLSharedEvent.
- vkExportMetalObjectsEXT: MTLDevice, MTLTexture (image or view),
  IOSurface and MTLSharedEvent. Command queue and buffer exports return
  NULL; KosmicKrisp uses an MTL4 queue.

Local experiment for the native Alyx path, not an upstream submission.

